hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20624","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Rabi'ah ibn Laqit, from Abd Allah ibn Hawalah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is saved from three is saved, three times: my death, the Dajjal, and the killing of a caliph patient upon the truth, giving it."
"20625","Abu Sa'id the freedman of Banu Hashim and Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Makhul narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hawalah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be an army in Sham and an army in Yemen. A man said: Choose for me, O Messenger of Allah, when that comes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adhere to Sham, adhere to Sham, three times, adhere to Sham. Whoever refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its pools, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has guaranteed me Sham and its people. Abu al-Nadr said: Twice: let him join his Yemen."
